---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"; import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro"; import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Book Ownership, Rights and Publishing Control" description="Understand the Author Vista position on copyright, royalties, publishing accounts, licensed assets and author approval.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Ownership and control" title="Your book remains yours." intro="Author Vista provides professional expertise and production support. You retain ownership of your work and the royalties generated through your publishing accounts." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell split"><div><p class="eyebrow">What the author retains</p><h2>Control should be visible in the agreement and the process.</h2></div><div><ul class="rule-list"><li><strong>01</strong><span>Copyright in the manuscript and book content.</span></li><li><strong>02</strong><span>Approved source files, subject to agreed licensing terms.</span></li><li><strong>03</strong><span>Publishing and platform accounts wherever the platform permits.</span></li><li><strong>04</strong><span>Royalties and commercial rights to the finished book.</span></li></ul></div></div></section>
  <section class="section surface-ivory"><div class="shell editorial-split"><div><p class="eyebrow">What must be defined</p><h2>The important details should never be hidden in a slogan.</h2><div class="prose"><p>The client agreement must explain ISBN ownership, editable working files, licensed fonts, stock images, illustration rights and audiobook rights. Those details can vary by asset, provider and project.</p><p>For that reason, Author Vista does not promise “100% ownership of everything.” It promises to make the applicable ownership and licensing terms clear before engagement.</p></div></div><div class="service-motif motif-marks" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>AV</b></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="answer-block"><p class="eyebrow">Publishing identity</p><h2>Who controls the publishing account?</h2><p>The intended model is for the author to hold and control the publishing account wherever the chosen platform permits. Author Vista may provide preparation and submission assistance, but it does not require publication under an account controlled by Author Vista.</p></div></div></section>
  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
